cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the paper."
title: "AdvJudge-Zero: Binary Decision Flips in LLM-as-a-Judge via Adversarial Control Tokens"
type: conference-paper
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Tung-Ling
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Yuhao
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Hongliang
version: "camera-ready"
identifiers:
  - type: arxiv
    value: "2512.17375"
    description: "Preprint record; repository accompanies the NeurIPS 2026 camera-ready revision."
abstract: >-
  We introduce AdvJudge-Zero, a zero-seed beam search over a judge's own
  next-token distribution that discovers short, low-perplexity response strings
  that flip binary judgments. We evaluate replacement and append-only attacks,
  filtering, mechanism-stratified hardening, and GRPO behavior.
keywords:
  - LLM-as-a-Judge
  - reward hacking
  - adversarial robustness
  - reinforcement learning
conference:
  name: "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems"
